  ;; but that path requires foreign-method re-entry from inside a
  ;; native method and isn't yet wired — throws TypeError for
  ;; non-Set arguments. One shared function; all
  ;; seven ids point at it, branching internally on method_id (matches
  ;; the shared validation + pressure pre-check the original branch
